## 5. AUTHENTICATION & RBAC

### 5.1 Auth requirements (all server-enforced)

- Register (customer or vendor application), sign in, sign out, session retrieval, email verification, forgot password, reset password.
- Password hashing: **scrypt** (N=16384, r=8, p=1, 16-byte random salt, 64-byte key) or argon2id — with `timingSafeEqual`. Dummy-hash verification on unknown emails so timing cannot enumerate accounts.
- Sessions: signed opaque tokens (`rawToken.hmacSha256`), HttpOnly + Secure (production) + SameSite=Lax cookies, 7-day TTL, **stored only as SHA-256 hashes**, revocable server-side; password reset revokes all sessions.
- Email verification and password-reset tokens: single-use, hashed at rest, expiring (24h / 30m).
- Brute-force lockout: 5 consecutive failures → 15-minute lockout (429).
- Rate limiting on auth, checkout, and mutating endpoints (per-IP buckets in Redis or `rate_limit_counters`).
- Server-side Zod validation on every request; safe error messages; generic responses that never leak account existence where required.
- CSRF: SameSite cookies + double-submit token on state-changing requests. CORS restricted to the storefront origin. Security headers: CSP (no `unsafe-eval`), HSTS, X-Frame-Options/frame-ancestors 'none', Referrer-Policy.
- Guest browsing and guest carts supported (server-held anonymous session id; guest cart merges into the customer cart on sign-in, re-priced at merge).
- **Identity is derived server-side from the verified session — never from a client-asserted header or body field.**

### 5.2 RBAC role matrix (server-side capability checks on every route)

| Role | Scope |
|---|---|
| CUSTOMER | own profile, addresses, cart, checkout, own orders (view/cancel/refund-request), wishlist, notifications |
| VENDOR | own profile (gated on onboarding APPROVED), own products CRUD + submit-for-review, own inventory, own order lines + fulfilment updates, own summaries |
| ADMIN_SUPER | everything |
| CATALOG_MANAGER | products, gemstones, settings, taxonomy, media (approve/reject/publish/unpublish/archive) |
| CONTENT_EDITOR | content, navigation, SEO (write; cannot approve/publish) |
| CONTENT_PUBLISHER | content + approve/publish (two-person rule with editor) |
| COMMERCE_OPERATOR | orders, refunds (approve/execute), inventory, fulfilment oversight |
| TRUST_REVIEWER | review queues for anomalies and flagged records |
| CONCIERGE_AGENT | assigned conversations, customer read |
| AI_OPERATIONS | conversations, tool-call audit, evaluations, guardrails |
| MIGRATION_ENGINEER | import batches, conflicts, derived approvals |
| READ_ONLY_ANALYST | dashboards only, PII-free by role |

Rules: policy denial = **403 with an internal reason only** (rule text never returned); separation of duties — **a vendor can never approve or publish their own product**; CMS approval is two-person (editor ≠ approver); every privileged mutation writes `audit_logs` with before and after state; audit write failure fails the action closed.

