### 7.12 Live catalogue integration — gemstock.org (actual product supply)

The storefront's gemstones are **real products fetched from [gemstock.org](https://gemstock.org)** — an established Bangkok gem-dealer house (GEMSTOCK.ORG COMPANY LIMITED, Jewelry Trade Center, Silom Road, Bangkok — the same bourse quarter as the Maihan Bangkok salon). Build a first-class **catalogue ingestion pipeline** against it:

- **What gemstock.org actually publishes (observed):** collection pages per gem type and sub-variety (Emerald, Tourmaline, Sapphire, Spinel, Ruby, Garnet, Alexandrite, Tanzanite, Topaz, Zircon, Beryl, Chrysoberyl, Kunzite, Moonstone, Morganite, Opal, Peridot, Quartz, Pearls, Diamonds…), with deep colour collections (e.g. Sapphire → Royal Blue / Cornflower Blue / Padparadscha / Pink / Yellow / Teal / Parti; Ruby → Pigeon's Blood / Star; Spinel → Cobalt Blue / Mahenge / Vivid Red; Paraíba → Neon Blue / Neon Green), shape filters (cushion, pear, heart, octagon, oval, radiant), price-band filters (< $1k up to > $200k), a Jewellery collection (rings, pendants, brooches), and product pages carrying: full title with carats + cut + colour + origin, **price and price-per-carat**, multiple photos, availability (`free worldwide shipping` vs **"Item is sold"**), and descriptive copy.
- **Ingestion:** a deterministic, idempotent **sync service** (worker job + manual admin trigger) crawls/fetches the collection and product pages (respect `robots.txt`, rate-limit politely ~1 request / 2s, identify with a proper UA), parses each product into the canonical catalogue rows: `gemstones` (gem_ref, carat, shape, colour, origin, treatment when stated, price_amount, price_per_carat, availability incl. sold), products with kind=LOOSE_STONE (and jewellery items as READY_MADE), plus `assets` + `asset_usages` for photos (media imported into your own storage/CDN with a content hash — never hotlinked at runtime).
- **Idempotency & freshness:** upsert keyed on the source product URL/id; re-sync updates price/availability/sold-status; sold items remain visible but marked **SOLD** with an enquiry CTA; deletions on the source are soft-flagged, never hard-deleted. Every sync run records an `import_batches` row (count, added/updated/sold-marked/errors) visible in the admin back office.
- **Provenance & honesty:** every synced product carries `source_url` pointing to the gemstock.org product page, `evidence_status='OBSERVED'` for parsed fields, and **UNKNOWN for anything the source does not state** (clarity, dimensions, treatment…) — rendered as "Not evidenced", never invented. DYO compatibility uses the synced stones exactly like native ones.
- **Fallback:** when gemstock.org is unreachable or rate-limits you, the storefront keeps serving the last synced snapshot and the admin sees the sync failure — the site never renders fake products in its place.
- **Seed:** the initial database seed IS a gemstock.org sync (plus the reference vocabulary); the builder should ship a small offline fixture copy of synced products only for tests/CI, clearly marked as fixture data.

