## 10. SECURITY CHECKLIST (implementation-level)

- [ ] Server-side session on every protected operation; no client-asserted identity/role headers trusted in production.
- [ ] Ownership predicates on every resource read/mutation (customer↔own orders/profile/addresses/wishlist; vendor↔own products/order-lines; admin capability per module).
- [ ] Horizontal/vertical privilege escalation + IDOR tests (cross-customer order read = 403; cross-vendor edit = 403; customer refund-approve = 403; non-admin on admin routes = 401/403).
- [ ] Mass-assignment protection (strict Zod schemas; unknown fields rejected).
- [ ] SQL injection surface eliminated (parameterised queries/query builder only; identifiers whitelisted).
- [ ] XSS: React escaping; any rich text sanitised against an explicit tag allow-list; never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with unsanitised input.
- [ ] Uploads: presigned direct-to-storage; content sniffing not extension; type/size caps; virus scan seam; EXIF stripped; storage keys server-generated.
- [ ] Webhooks: raw-body HMAC before parse; timestamp tolerance; idempotent receipts; no payload-URL following; amounts re-derived server-side.
- [ ] Secrets: platform secret manager only; never in repo/DB/logs/traces; leaked secret = rotate first.
- [ ] PII: never in logs, metrics, analytics, embeddings, or event payloads; redaction before any log/model call.
- [ ] Rate limits on auth + mutating endpoints; fail closed on money/trust/authorization; fail open only on cache.
- [ ] Every privileged mutation audited (before/after) — audit failure fails the action.
- [ ] Appraisal/certificate documents private; short-lived signed URLs only.
- [ ] Production error responses leak nothing (no stack, no SQL, no driver text).

