## 11. PERFORMANCE & ACCESSIBILITY

- Server components by default; client islands only for interaction (configurator, cart, AR/3D, forms); route-level `loading.tsx` skeletons (`aria-busy`), no spinners.
- Initial-JS budgets enforced (category route ≤ 170 KB gzip, product route ≤ 190 KB gzip) with a CI check.
- `next/image` (or equivalent) + remote patterns for catalogue imagery; lazy 3D/AR bundles; request cancellation; resource cleanup (WebGL contexts, media streams, timers).
- Postgres indexes on every filtered/sorted column; no N+1 in catalogue/order flows (batch or lateral joins).
- WCAG 2.2 AA: semantic HTML, keyboard-complete journeys (mega-menu, drawers, modals, configurator), focus rings, labels + error associations, alt text, contrast ≥ 4.5:1, status not colour-only, screen-reader announcements for important changes, `prefers-reduced-motion`.

